@@ -201,6 +201,7 @@ Legend: `[x]` done in code · `[~]` partly done / needs your device to confirm 
 | 0218 | 2026-11-02 | CloudKit item 8 leftover: **another register creates a missing Shopify order** (your request: do the rest of the docs). The problem found first: today the shared sale row is written after the order, so a sale left in a dead iPad's queue leaves no trace anywhere. So with CloudKit on the outbox gets an `early` step that writes the sale before the receipt and the order (CloudKit only, sales only, not in practice mode; a failure is not fatal and the final entry step writes it again with the order on it); `runItem` now returns the finished sale and the entry fields come from one helper. `orderRecovery.ts` has the rules (stranded sale, claim handle and fields, stale claims, the gift card exception, the notice); `cloudkit/orderRecoverySync.ts` is the job: at most every ten minutes, three sales per run, a write-once claim first (so two registers cannot both create it), then `runItem` on the sale, then a notice. Run from `pollShared`. New `tests/orderrecovery.test.ts` (14 tests). Guesses and known gaps under 0218. |
 | 0219 | 2026-11-02 | CloudKit patch 6e: **the owner-only CloudKit export** (your request: do the rest of the docs), plus corrections. The export: `exportAll.ts` is the pure half (the list of every record type, `readAll` that reads a whole list and fails loudly, `collectExport` that builds the files, manifest and README, `zipExport` with fflate); `exportAllIO.ts` writes the zip to the cache folder, adds the logo picture, and refuses in a practice run; the Cloud sync page has an owner-only **Back up everything** button that confirms first and shares the zip. New `tests/exportall.test.ts` (9 tests) and `tests/lazybackend.test.ts` (3 tests). **Corrections to earlier patches, found by a real type check and by installing `fflate` so the whole suite ran:** (1) the tsc setup in this repo does not check anything here (`expo/tsconfig.base` is missing), so the "tsc clean" I reported for 0213 to 0218 meant nothing. I ran a lenient check of every file I touched and it found two real bugs in 0216: `migrationPanel.ts` read `phase` from a failure result that has none (a failed count check), and `CloudSync.tsx` used `useApp` without importing it. Both fixed here, with tests. (2) With `fflate` installed the suite showed two failures in `demoguard.test.ts` that my patches caused: 0215 put `put()` calls in `sync.ts` outside the guarded seam, and the new export wrote a file with no guard. The direct backend handles now live in `cloudkit/lazyBackend.ts` (the write stops on the same guard as the seam) and the export checks the guard. With `fflate` installed the whole suite passes (1868, 0 failing). |
 | 0220 | 2026-11-02 | CloudKit patch 8: **the switch** (your request: do the rest of the docs). Rules in `backendChoice.ts` (flag values, start-up kind, when to move, which of a till's own sales are the gap, what the page says), job in `cloudkit/backendSwitch.ts` (`install`, `check`, `rollBack`, `allowSwitch`, `view`), flag storage in `cloudkit/backendFlagIO.ts` (guarded, local). `App.tsx` now installs the backend through the switch instead of always Shopify; `pollShared` calls `backendSwitch.check()` first. Cloud sync page: where this till keeps shared data, with the rollback and its way back. **Decisions made here, in GUESSES:** cut over in one go (no dual-write); a switched till never falls back by itself; the gap is closed by sending a till's own recent sales, not by dual-writing. **Not done:** retiring the 25 s poll, which needs CloudKit subscriptions in Swift (8b). New `tests/backendchoice.test.ts` (9 tests) and `tests/backendswitch.test.ts` (11 tests); full suite 1891, 0 failing with `fflate` installed; a lenient type check of the new files is clean. |
+| 0234 | 2026-11-11 | Import fix, found on the first real run in Development: **Back up everything** stopped with an error about the Square history, and the sync chip kept changing. CloudKit's Development schema only gets a record type when something first writes it, and a list of a type that does not exist yet throws `unknownItem` ("Did not find record type"). `runQuery` in `CloudKitSyncModule.swift` now returns an empty list for that case, so the backup, the polls and the count check treat a type nothing has written as empty. One pin test in `tests/cloudkitswift.test.ts`. **The Swift is not compiled.** Needs a rebuild (`npm run ios`). Whether this also settles the chip is not confirmed: the chip shows whichever of many background jobs wrote the shared sync state last. | Import |
 | 0233 | 2026-11-11 | Import fix, found on the first real import into Development: it stopped at the sales step with `invalid attempt to set value type STRING for field 'cogs_cents' for type 'Sale', defined to be: NUMBER_INT64`. A Shopify row holds every value as text, and a row with no readable `sale_json` was written field by field as it came, so its amounts went up as text into a type whose amounts are numbers. `saleWriteFromFields` now turns every `*_cents` field that is a whole number into a number on that path. One test in `tests/salerecords.test.ts`. If a sale already wrote a text amount into Development, that field's type is already wrong there: reset the Development environment's `Sale` type (see the checklist). | Import |
 | 0232 | 2026-11-11 | Build fix, found on the first launch on iPad (iOS 27.0.1): the app crashed at launch with `UIApplicationEvaluateRuntimeIssueForNoSceneLifecycleAdoption`, because iOS 27 requires the UIScene lifecycle for apps built with its SDK and Expo SDK 54's AppDelegate makes the window itself. `plugins/withCloudKit.js` now adds the scene manifest to Info.plist, stops the AppDelegate starting React Native, and appends a `SceneDelegate` to `AppDelegate.swift` that makes the window, starts React Native, hands URLs and universal links back to the AppDelegate's methods, and records CloudKit share links (`userDidAcceptCloudKitShareWith` on the scene, `cloudKitShareMetadata` on a cold launch), because iOS no longer calls the AppDelegate's version under scenes. Five tests in `tests/cloudkitplugin.test.ts`; a real `expo prebuild` was run and the output read. **The Swift is not compiled and has not run on a device.** Expo's own fix is SDK 57 or later; this is a workaround on SDK 54. Needs `npm run ios:reset`. | Build |
 | 0231 | 2026-11-11 | Build fix, found on the first Mac build (Xcode 27, iOS 27.2 SDK). `plugins/withCloudKit.js` now adds a loop to the Podfile's `post_install` that lifts any pod target below iOS 15.0 to the app's 17.0, because Xcode 27 refuses to build below 15.0 and three resource bundles (RNDeviceInfo 9.0, RNCAsyncStorage 13.4, RNSVG 12.4) still said less. Two tests in `tests/cloudkitplugin.test.ts`. Needs `npm run ios:reset` to regenerate `ios/`. Not run through a real prebuild here. | Build |
